course: dictionary
lesson: 8167
title: Residence: where you live
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A residence is a formal word for a home: a house or building where someone lives. Official writing and forms use it, while everyday talk says «home» or «house».
explain: Toad, in The Wind in the Willows, describes his house like an estate agent's advert: «an eligible self-contained gentleman's residence very unique». The fancy words are a clue. Toad is showing off, and «residence» sounds grander than just «house».
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Place of residence» means where you live. «Official residence» means a special home linked to a job, like 10 Downing Street. «In residence» means living or working at a place right now.
fact: Residence means a house or building where someone lives, especially a large or official one.
fact: Residence can also mean the fact of living in a place, as in «take up residence», which means move in.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, a hall of residence is a building where university students live.
fact: «In residence» means living or working at a place, as in «writer in residence».
fact: «Residence» is a formal word. In everyday talk, people say «home» or «house».
exercise: Toad calls his house «an eligible self-contained gentleman's residence». What is a residence? | A road outside the town | A type of bird | A shop that sells sweets | *A house where someone lives
exercise: On a form, you are asked for your «place of residence». What do they want to know? | Your favourite food | *Where you live | The name of your teacher | Your school's sports team
exercise: «The students live in the hall of residence.» Where do the students live? | On a fishing boat | In a barn on a farm | *In a building for university students | In a tent at a festival
test: Which phrase means living or working at a place right now? | *In residence | In the garden | At the seaside | Out of order
test: Which word is the everyday word for a residence? | *House | Dragon | Trolley | Tractor
exam: Which sentence uses «residence» correctly? | Residence is a kind of sandwich | *The minister moved into her official residence in London | The residence ate all the cake | I went residence to the shop for milk
